Author: Run Edit Run fleet <fleet@runeditrun.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 10 20:18:38 2026 +1000

    fix: an unavailable shared record's refusal survives a late list load
    
    SharedRecords held one error for both the list read and the open-record read,
    so a successful list load cleared the 'Record is unavailable' alert set by a
    403 on opening a record. The list error and the open-record error are now
    separate state; a list load clears only its own error, and the open error
    clears when another record is opened, the detail closes, the type or search
    changes, or the open succeeds. A browser regression holds the list response
    until the 403 has landed and asserts the alert stays.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

